{"kind":"assert","text":"Read-only S1 preparation: check late-opening disposal mode\n\nAt current main 9d96cf25, OAuthHttpLayers.abrupt clears its map and arranges abrupt disposal of an opening result. The awaiting open method sees the missing layer and calls close with its default remove-sessions disposition. That may arrange a later closeAll after abrupt. McpHttp.closeAll removes durable session rows, while abrupt and detach retain them. The existing late-opening case in oauth-http.scope.test.ts exercises closeGrant(id,true), not abrupt during the opening. This is a source hypothesis, not a confirmed hosted defect.\n\nBefore S1 implementation, run one deterministic component probe from scratch against the unmodified production OAuthHttpLayers and McpHttp classes. Use explicit standing, Wire and session-store stand-ins with synthetic TEST rows. Compare late abrupt disposal with late detach, ordinary abrupt after opening, and graceful close during opening. Record actual call order and row state. Join any close promise the production manager actually starts; never call closeAll as probe cleanup, since that would contaminate retained-row observations. No sleeps, provider call, hosted endpoint, signing key, invitation, deployment or source edit.\n\nThe result supplies witness selection for request e39e7cef only. It does not start an S1 implementation branch or change order 8a78f701: M4 still goes through review first. Record exact source hashes, node exit and source continuity. No gate or source seal changes. Builder only; planner deploys. Never run rm -rf or rm -f.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}